  <DataPropertyAssertion>
    <DataProperty abbreviatedIRI="kt:description"/>
    <NamedIndividual abbreviatedIRI="kt:issue-nondeterministic-data-values"/>
    <Literal>A data value that only follows from a non-deterministic branch (for example one branch of a union or an at-most restriction) is treated as a candidate and verified lazily. The realizing item queues a satisfiability test of the individual together with the negated value (individual and not(SOME(dataProperty,{value}))) and caches the result per (individual, data property, value); only values whose negation is unsatisfiable are published. The verification uses temporary SOME concepts in the ontology of the realizing item, so no answerer state is needed. Deterministic values, including TBox-derived hasValue and minimum cardinality values, are answered without a test.</Literal>
  </DataPropertyAssertion>

