    <Literal>Fixed. The existential interpretation remains config-gated (Konclude.Answering.InterpretNonAnswerIndividualVariablesAsAnonymousVariables); the single-variable boolean ASK reduction is skipped so named witnesses work with the default config. A closed ASK is answered directly from the conjunction of its boolean sub-queries, and non-closed sub-queries use query-local placeholders for hidden individual variables while preserving direct-result streaming. The regular resolver path is covered by the *-regular tests with Konclude.Answering.ClosedAskDirectBooleanAnswering=false. Regression guards include kt:sparql-ask-class-assertion, kt:sparql-ask-complex, kt:sparql-ask-anonymous-woman, kt:sparql-ask-anonymous-child, kt:sparql-ask-anonymous-woman-child, kt:sparql-ask-anonymous-man, kt:sparql-select-anonymous-woman and kt:sparql-select-hidden-anonymous-join. See Docs/Analysis-SPARQL-ASK-ClassAssertion.md.</Literal>
