    <Literal>A variable-predicate query over constant individuals (for example SELECT ?p { sp:alice ?p sp:bob } or SELECT ?d ?v { sp:alice ?d ?v }) answers empty. The parser classifies the pattern as an object-property or data-property SCHEMA query (property hierarchy) instead of a fact query over the known subject/object, so the role/data-property variable never becomes a binding. The object-property path is the allObjPropVars branch; the data-property path is the allDataPropVars branch in CSPARQLRedlandRasqalReasoningBGPQueryParser::generateBGPBasedSubQueries. Affects kt:sparql-select-role-variable and kt:sparql-select-data-variable. See Docs/Investigation-SPARQL-VariablePredicate.md.</Literal>
